{
  "id": "L45",
  "subnivel": "A2.2",
  "unidad": 12,
  "titulo": "Tengo que",
  "explicacion": [
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "**have to** + verbo significa «tener que». Expresa una obligación. Con he, she, it cambia a **has to**."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "I / You / We / They",
          "have to",
          "I have to work on Saturday."
        ],
        [
          "He / She / It",
          "has to",
          "She has to wear a uniform."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "El negativo **don't have to** no es una prohibición: significa «no es necesario»."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "I don't have to work tomorrow.",
          "No tengo que trabajar mañana."
        ],
        [
          "He doesn't have to wear a uniform.",
          "No tiene que usar uniforme."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "Después de **doesn't** y de **does** se usa **have to**, no has to: *He doesn't have to*, *Does he have to?*"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "La pregunta se hace con Do o Does:"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "Do you have to work tonight?",
          "Yes, I do.",
          "No, I don't."
        ],
        [
          "Does she have to study?",
          "Yes, she does.",
          "No, she doesn't."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "El pasado es **had to** para todas las personas: *Yesterday I had to work late.*"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "Trabajo y pendientes:"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "columnas": [
        "Inglés",
        "Español"
      ],
      "filas": [
        [
          "task",
          "pendiente, tarea"
        ],
        [
          "report",
          "reporte"
        ],
        [
          "send",
          "enviar"
        ],
        [
          "answer",
          "contestar"
        ],
        [
          "print",
          "imprimir"
        ],
        [
          "uniform",
          "uniforme"
        ],
        [
          "on time",
          "a tiempo"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
